add("BG014","M106",3,"The product measure dx is finite on compact subsets of V.",[[d+"0/definition","dx is the finite product of real Lebesgue factor measures."],[inp+"0/statement","The coordinate type is finite."]],"For Measure.pi.isFiniteMeasureOnCompacts, each factor is sigma-finite by BG013 and finite on compact sets by BG012, with the stated measurable and topological structures. These discharge the full probed telescope, including its sigma-finiteness premises.");
add("BG015","M122",3,"For every real vector v, the square of its D002 norm equals the finite sum of the squares of its coordinates.",[[d+"1/definition","The norm is the square root of that finite sum."]],"The radicand is nonnegative by real square nonnegativity and finite sums. Real.sq_sqrt therefore applies. This rewrites e as a finite polynomial in coordinate derivatives. It also justifies the coordinate norm comparison in S003: each coordinate square is at most the full sum, hence |x_j|≤|x| by nonnegative real square comparison.");
